notes[2]['text']='The handwritten Appendix is attributed on the page to P. Deligne. Its cancelled title has readable Existence de point with uncertain final s; the d\x27/Un cancellation boundary remains uncertain. The revised phrase appears to state Un topos cohérent a suffisamment de points, with local a and final punctuation doubts. This is a contents title, not a proof.'.replace('\\x27',"'")
notes[5]['text']='The third cancelled paragraph calls the rédaction of sections 1–3 àomplète as typed, with a separate m/p superposition. It proposes examples: a locally algebraic but nonalgebraic topos, a separately cancelled noncoherent morphism between coherent topoi, and a bottom insertion about a generating family of coherent objects and failure of local algebraicity. The final s in objet(s) and the bottom insertion’s cancellation state remain uncertain. These examples are named, not constructed or verified on this sheet.'
notes[6]['text']='Long pencil cancellation strokes visibly traverse all three lower typed paragraphs. A diagonal also crosses the bottom insertion; its live/cancelled state is retained as a doubt, without assigning chronology. The left double stroke, short appendix mark, left brace and relocation curve are reproduced in TikZ. Hand attribution is not independently established; the inventory uses another unnamed hand for handwriting.'
notes.append(dict(id='s018-main-note09',text='The same-letter repeated S and B use mathbb under the supplied typescript convention. Separate c/x, s/f, u/y/g, p/b/l, t/r and m/p superpositions retain uncertain order. The red o in tomber has an uncertain l/i underprint. H expressly omits typewriter superpositions, so these rows describe a scope difference as well as a fuller diplomatic reading.',basis='Main inspected the heading, NB, faisceaux, àomplète and tomber crops; documentary comparison only.'))
notes.append(dict(id='s018-main-note10',text='Sommaire is visibly underlined, whereas H encodes italic emphasis; H’s supplied style uses normalem and does not turn emph into an underline. The source capital L in Lim and separate hand arrow are preserved. Three raised o abbreviations each carry an underline. These are visible state/letter differences, not prose dash or ellipsis code differences.',basis='Main title, Lim and three numéro crops; local reading of supplied H style only, without external research.'))
notes.append(dict(id='s018-main-note11',text='The top pencil references remain pale; lower 3.1 is resolved. No dash is securely visible between 2.9 and à. The proposed old 2 under the 3 of 38 is rejected because a separate complete 2 is not established by the retraced strokes. The cancelled phrase after On peut visibly ends à la rigue, without a restored ur.',basis='Main top-note, right ranges and rigue crops; shape and spacing decisions, no semantic completion.'))
